    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe unchanged TB371FC production kernel now reaches the SPSS PIL probe, then aborts on its 32-bit store to `0x01881028`. The preceding qualified LLCC binary reports `pil_tz_driver_probe+0x6bc/0x788`, opcode `STR W8,[X10]`, with W8=`0xfcffffff`. The actual full DT names this exact four-byte resource `sp2soc_irq_mask` and supplies event bits 24 and 25.\n\n## Changes\n\nAdd the default-off `qcom-sm8250-spss-irq-mask` device and one four-byte board mapping. Explicitly enabling it retains the complete guest-written mask and a separate programmed flag. Unknown reset state and explicitly programmed zero remain distinct. All MMIO reads and invalid delivered writes return errors. IRQ delivery, READY, clocks, timers, firmware and PAS authentication remain outside this device.\n\nVersion-1 migration stores exactly 25 bytes and checks the profile, `SPM1` identity, geometry, canonical flag and unknown/disabled state invariants. Existing QSEE and other SPSS resource ownership is unchanged.\n\nTwo pinned source inputs generate the address, bit positions and probe mask. Complete input length, SHA-256 and Git blob identity are checked before generation. The new verifier retries only transient HTTP 429/5xx or timeouts, at most three attempts; identity failures are final. Earlier source verifiers are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Local source generation reproduced both outputs from both complete pinned files. Both one-bit source tampering attempts were rejected; parser and mocked transport checks are recorded separately.\n- Static model and MMIO dispatch reviews are recorded. Scalar eight-byte and unaligned accesses reach a single rejecting callback; a five-byte buffered write may commit the valid four-byte prefix before its neighboring hole fails. The compiled test checks these different outcomes.\n- The new component gate requires 21 groups, three completed migrations, both profile mismatch directions, six single-bit corrupted-stream rejections, four original streams and six mutated copies. Every successful restore starts with 18 pure QOM getters after a genuinely dirtied destination.\n- All prior 98 gate contracts, commands and relative order are preserved. Two additions make the current plan 95 component plus five Linux gates, with the existing A77/PCI UFS and active/suspended Linux UFS checks retained.\n- Local harness validation ran all 33 unit tests: 32 passed and the existing socket/symlink fixture test errored because this environment rejects `socket(AF_UNIX)` with EPERM. Its original log is retained. The separate 14 plan tests passed. Formal Linux CI still requires all 33 tests without skips.\n\nThe original SPSS head `3bd583f2079634d01c12160ab3e3f0c5a3e47e86` completed both push and PR CI and all six independent audits of its actual push artifact. Those results remain bound to that exact head. Native execution was not started: the base branch advanced while the final qualification was being assembled.\n\nThe current head `a3a6183d4e9842b2e61d3d1c9cd7b69b44165187` merges mainline's public source download retry change, preserving both parents. The only overlap was `tb371fc/docs/ci.md`; both sections are retained, and the shared retry policy is explicitly limited to its seven consumers. All 29 other SPSS publication files, all 100 gate contracts and all source model/test pins are unchanged. Original Git modes, including the two executable verifiers, are preserved.\n\nThe combined head is undergoing its own push run [45517859568](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/actions/runs/45517859568) and PR run [45517869441](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/actions/runs/45517869441). Its actual artifact must pass all six audits before binding the unchanged-original-input diagnostic. The preceding LLCC run was a zero-LUN kernel-failure diagnostic; Android userspace, UI and boot completion remain unobserved.\n\n[The original SPSS CI and six-audit evidence](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/tree/8b7afa5dc97e40be44b081ed7de4d4f3b391c36e/tb371fc/evidence/spss-3bd583f-ci-20261125-6a5) includes the observed base-branch change; it is not a qualification of the combined head.\n\nCurrent base: `d40638391637e918f3382092d64fba0a7a17cade` (the original SPSS base was `7372681f546a7ac1b816377480601ddd8e7c16f5`). The preceding LLCC qualification and actual next frontier are retained at [the pinned evidence commit](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/tree/253e3b630bc7a4d2250dec6efcb36f764a605446/tb371fc/evidence/llcc-c02f3d7-ci-20261124-6a5).\n",
